#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:2
msgid "Filesystem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:4
msgid ""
"Simple filesystem read/write is achieved using the ``uv_fs_*`` functions "
"and the ``uv_fs_t`` struct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:9
msgid ""
"The libuv filesystem operations are different from :doc:`socket "
"operations <networking>`. Socket operations use the non-blocking "
"operations provided by the operating system. Filesystem operations use "
"blocking functions internally, but invoke these functions in a `thread "
"pool`_ and notify watchers registered with the event loop when "
"application interaction is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:18
msgid ""
"All filesystem functions have two forms - *synchronous* and "
"*asynchronous*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:20
msgid ""
"The *synchronous* forms automatically get called (and **block**) if the "
"callback is null. The return value of functions is a :ref:`libuv error "
"code <libuv-error-handling>`. This is usually only useful for synchronous"
" calls. The *asynchronous* form is called when a callback is passed and "
"the return value is 0."
msgstr ""

